option for fixing https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109193. \r\n\r\nThe core of the issue is twofold:\r\n1. When doing code completion for an object that is the return value of a function, GDScript will actually call the function if it is `const` so it can do code completion on for that object\r\n2. `RenderingServer.create_local_rendering_device()` is marked as const. And is technically const, but it does allocate a bunch of CPU and GPU resources and is not ref counted so it never gets freed\r\n\r\nI opted to solve the issue by removing `const` from `create_local_rendering_device()` since it doesn't really need it.\r\n\r\nI am worried that this will break compatibility for GDExtensions. If it does, and we can't accept the breakage, then perhaps there is a way for us to modify code complete to cache the return values of functions that it calls so we don't endlessly leak memory.\r\n\r\nCC @HolonProduction ","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098082,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwODI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdscript","name":"topic:gdscript","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:edi